d (KWin at least), so there's a significant impact there.\nBut for 4.6 an `#ifdef` makes sense so we solve the regression, and we can look into generalizing this logic for 4.7.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783375572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783386496","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115246#issuecomment-3783386496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115246","id":3783386496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hgeWA","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T09:24:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T09:24:53Z","body":"> Well it actually fixed resizing windows during splash on Wayland, so there's a significant impact there.\n\nI can't reproduce it, Wayland window seems to be non-resizable while splash is shown, and X11 resizes, but not redraw (same as before the change). So it was not fully fixed.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783386496/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783390989","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115246#issuecomment-3783390989","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115246","id":3783390989,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hgfcN","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T09:25:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T09:25:54Z","body":"On sway I still see no difference, neither in bootup times nor resizing (it always resized). I agree to look into this for 4.7. I can make a more thorough investigation now that I've got a good way of trying every compositor (build container and Fedora VM).\n\nFWIW, I'd propose figuring out a definitive way of handling splash on desktops. At least here on sway the drawing is still stalled.\n\nNo idea about other desktops, but on Wayland we could put the splash on a subsurface (with the chosen background) until loading is done.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783390989/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783399375","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115246#issuecomment-3783399375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115246","id":3783399375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hghfP","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T09:27:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T09:27:51Z","body":"> but on Wayland it's not redrawing the window until getting any event (e.g, mouse move over the window)\n\nThat's interesting and somewhat familiar. There's probably something happening with the event loop (or the frame timeout loop) that's keeping a mutex locked.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783399375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783419680","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115246#issuecomment-3783419680","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115246","id":3783419680,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hgmcg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T09:32:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T09:32:46Z","body":"> No idea about other desktops, but on Wayland we could put the splash on a subsurface (with the chosen background) until loading is done.\n\nSomething like this can be done on macOS as well, but won't do much since currently `Main::start` is blocking main thread and all UI processing always happen on main thread.\n\nIt probably better to not block, and do waiting in the main event loop, while it running normally, but without calling `Main::iteration` until wait is over. This should also allow redrawing it on every event loop iteration and should fix resizing it on window resize.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783419680/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783453418","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115246#issuecomment-3783453418","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115246","id":3783453418,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hgurq","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T09:40:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T09:40:53Z","body":"> > Well it actually fixed resizing windows during splash on Wayland, so there's a significant impact there.\n> \n> I can't reproduce it, Wayland window seems to be non-resizable while splash is shown, and X11 resizes, but not redraw (same as before the change). So it was not fully fixed.\n\nThat's weird, it definitely worked for me when I tested #115118, but now it's broken again.\n\nBut now even go back to 1d34edf52 resizing doesn't work. ¯\\\\\\_(ツ)\\_/¯","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783453418/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783461560","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115246#issuecomment-3783461560","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115246","id":3783461560,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hgwq4","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T09:42:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T09:44:02Z","body":"TBCH, I'm not that surprised. AFAICT the issue is that we need to _always_ handle events and redraw to have a responsive splash screen. If the main thread is blocked on initialization and both the DS and renderer are not doing their job, it's always going to have issues.\n\nThat's why I've been thinking for a while to add some \"system offloaded\" splash logic, like by working with subsurfaces on wayland.\n\nEdit: oops, missed bruvgz's message which said a similar thing, sorry 😅","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783461560/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]